WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
Film Courage: I get so nervous…

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.080
Omari Hardwick: You get nervous?

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.430
I thought we [the actors] were the ones who
are supposed to be nervous?

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.430
Film Courage: Yeah.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:07.810
Omari Hardwick: Ground yourself.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:08.810
Grab onto something.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:09.810
Film Courage: Good idea.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:10.810
I will.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.990
Omari Hardwick: There you go.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:18.270
Film Courage: Omari, for other actors watching
your career right now you are making it look

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:23.570
very easy, which I know you’ve talked about
how it has not been easy for you.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:29.939
But you’re in SHOT CALLER movie, you’re
on the show POWER and you have all these projects

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:31.090
in the works.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.861
Let’s talk about the hypothetical LA friend
that a lot of us have who is a talented, hard

00:00:35.861 --> 00:00:40.770
working actor but they can’t get in a room
because they are not represented by the right

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:41.770
agency.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.690
What’s your advice for that person?

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:49.050
Omari Hardwick: Great way to start an interview,
first of all.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:56.350
That’s interesting because tonight (for
example) I am inviting friends who got off

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.690
the Hollywood Dream Bus with me.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:02.730
Who never were necessarily able to execute
anything.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.280
You know it’s interesting because they will
be at the screening tonight for this film

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.750
[SHOT CALLER with Omari Hardwick as Kutcher]
and it’s one of those things where we don’t

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:15.010
have the same level in common in conversation
as we once had because life has happened for

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.070
me differently.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:22.210
I had to really check in with myself in terms
of the team personality in me thought that

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:26.390
(and I’ve always been a part of sports)
everybody that got off the dream bus with

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:30.110
me and what I mean by that is around the same
month that you get off the Dream Bus and you

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:34.350
come to LA or New York to make things happen
you get a collective of friends and y’all

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:40.050
start to run the audition circuit and slowly
certain people’s pace slows down and others

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.520
keep going.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:48.320
My big thing is always (to the people that
I am inviting tonight and to as you said those

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:53.740
aspiring actors), my wisdom and advice was
always first and foremost, if you can wake

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:58.370
up without wanting to do this…you have one
morning where you wake up and go “Oh…I

00:01:58.370 --> 00:01:59.630
don’t really want to do this.”

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.050
I would say get out because it’s way too
difficult!

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:09.030
Somebody could ask me are there moments of
that being defined as being discouraged and

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.580
I will go No…everybody is discouraged.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:15.190
Everybody calls home and goes “I don’t
know if I should become a rocket scientist

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:21.140
or as a woman if I should continue in this
world of men and corporate spectrums or law

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.690
or medicine or what have you.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:27.570
People all get discouraged including myself
and asking Mom and Dad if I should come back

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:30.000
home (very early in my journey out here).

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.810
But I think in terms of the representation
part I decided to not (and this is really

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:38.060
my wisdom to them) to not really worry about
it.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:45.340
My thought was it looked like it was easier
for me than it was because I really pressed

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:51.181
hard at the craft, the work, the acting classes,
making sure that I was in martial arts classes

00:02:51.181 --> 00:02:56.270
if I could add that to the repertoire box
or the box of tools that I could dig into

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:59.370
if I needed to work on the piano because one
day I could play a character where I play

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.370
the piano.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:04.300
Just work on the craft and don’t necessarily
worry about the representation.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.300
It will find you.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.400
The right agent will find you.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.030
The right manager.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:12.020
But now am I struggling in terms of wanting
even bigger out of my career while there are

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.720
people not where I’m at going “You look
like you made it?”

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.630
I don’t know what ‘make it’ is?

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:17.630
I’m satisfied.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:23.910
I am so humbled and thankful to God that I’m
where I am at but it’s always more and so

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:29.440
if you focus on the more being attained by
making sure that you do more for yourself,

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.940
then I don’t necessarily think that the
representation should matter.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.540
Again, I think they definitely will always
find you.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.940
Film Courage: Excellent.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:37.940
Thank you.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:38.940
Wow!

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.190
Omari Hardwick: Thank you!

